review_comments:
I realized that this API has a time-of-check-time-of-use weakness: if there are two concurrent gPRC calls, each of them might pass the `CheckDeviceAllocation` call, but then `NodePrepareResources` for one gRPC call changes the state such that `CheckDeviceAllocation` for the other wouldn't pass anymore.

This cannot be solved without a global lock. Perhaps we want such a global lock? It reduces concurrency, but overall might make things simpler. It would be one less thing that DRA driver authors need to worry about. However, we then also need to consider how this would work when there are two concurrent instances of the driver (https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/129832) - we would have to use file locking with a well-defined file name.

@klueska @byako: thoughts?
